# Backend

See also: `docs/013_BACKEND_STANDARD.md`, `docs/006_API_SPEC.md`

## Layering

```
Route Handler (app/api)
  → validate DTO
  → authorize role
  → backend/services use-case
  → backend/repositories adapter
  → Supabase / Redis / OpenAI
```

## Rules

- Keep domain decisions in services
- Define repository interfaces; implement adapters separately
- Validate at the boundary (Zod or equivalent)
- Never trust client-supplied roles — read from server session/profile
- Structured errors with stable codes
- Idempotent writes for webhooks / payment-like events
- No PII in info logs; correlate `requestId`

## Contracts

- Document routes in `api/contracts.ts` when adding endpoints
- Keep OpenAPI notes under `api/` in sync with handlers
